1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.990
Before we start building reports, let's cover two essential concepts: measures and dimensions.

2
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.399
These are the building blocks of every dynamic data export report.

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.524
Measures are the numerical values you want to analyze. 

4
00:00:13.524 --> 00:00:16.648
Think of them as the "what" in your report.

5
00:00:16.648 --> 00:00:21.132
Examples include total screen time, battery consumption percentages,

6
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.866
or app crash counts.

7
00:00:22.866 --> 00:00:26.766
Measures answer the question, "what am I measuring?"

8
00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:30.413
Dimensions provide context to your measures. 

9
00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:34.065
They're the "how" or "why" behind your data.

10
00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:38.699
Dimensions include things like firmware version, app version, or device model.

11
00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:41.932
They tell you how your data is grouped and categorized.

12
00:00:43.066 --> 00:00:44.699
Here's a practical example.

13
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.758
Let's say you select "Screen time" and "Force close events" as your measure

14
00:00:50.758 --> 00:00:53.606
and "App names" as your dimension. 

15
00:00:53.606 --> 00:00:58.188
You would be able to see which apps cause the most crashes

16
00:00:58.189 --> 00:01:00.066
relative to their screen time.

17
00:01:00.066 --> 00:01:01.999
That's an actionable insight!

18
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.565
With this information, you can easily identify the apps or app versions problematic to the fleet

19
00:01:08.565 --> 00:01:12.199
and have them removed or updated immediately.

20
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:17.633
The key takeaway? Measures tell you what you're measuring.

21
00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:21.566
Dimensions tell you how that data is organized.

22
00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.927
Together, they help you answer specific 

23
00:01:24.927 --> 00:01:28.065
questions about your device fleet and user behavior.

24
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.333
Want to see this in action? 

25
00:01:30.766 --> 00:01:35.099
In the next video, we'll walk through creating your first report step-by-step. 

26
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:36.766
See you there!

